      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I would personally prefer this as a permission popup at the start of the world that acts as permission for the entire world (for that session). There may be some use cases for game worlds that might use specific avatars as part of the gameplay so having it on world start would avoid breaking the game flow or spoiling any specific moments, as well as making it possible for avatar changes during moments such as a player falling.\nHaving it at the start of a world would inform the player that it can happen in the world and allow them to save their choice for that session.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2022-07-31T18:12:15.059Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Currently, worlds with avatar pedestals can change the player's avatar whenever the pedestal is activated, whether by the player or by a script. However, interacting with an avatar pedestal can be accidental. Or a world can forcibly change the player's avatar to annoy them. In either case, having your avatar changed can be quite obnoxious and disorienting. Similarly to how portal confirmations have been added, it would be nice if avatar changes could be set to require confirmations before the change takes effect.",
